      "key": {
        "uuid": "553711bf_6fd9c099",
        "filename": "cmds/hid/src/com/android/commands/hid/Event.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 123,
      "author": {
        "id": 1149384
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-13T01:52:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can the register command in json contain that dict directly? So, something like:\n\n\"feature_reports\": [\n{ \"type\": 0x05,\n  \"data\": [0x05, 0x1e, 0x00, 0x05, 0x00, 0xe2, 0xff, 0xf2, 0x22, 0xbe, 0x22, 0x8d, 0x22, 0x4f, 0xdd, 0x4d,\n    0xdd, 0x39, 0xdd, 0x1c, 0x02, 0x1c, 0x02, 0xe3, 0x1f, 0x8b, 0xdf, 0x8c, 0x1e, 0xb4, 0xde, 0x30,\n    0x20, 0x71, 0xe0, 0x10, 0x00, 0xca, 0xfc, 0x64, 0x4d]\n  }\n]\n\nAlso, regarding the first byte being the report number : is that custom to Sony driver? Or is it the contract for all drivers? I\u0027m not able to find documentation about the report format anywhere. Since the report id is already being set separately, what is the value of copying that into the report?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 123,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 123,
        "endChar": 65
      },
      "revId": "51db903be0d5f780a74b7eb6cc38ffbe2f3a97db",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f9330a22_d7cab8ba",
        "filename": "cmds/hid/src/com/android/commands/hid/Event.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 123,
      "author": {
        "id": 1154383
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-13T04:53:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The first byte is generally speaking the report ID as documented in the HID spec (https://www.usb.org/sites/default/files/documents/hid1_11.pdf), see e.g. section 8.1 and 8.2. However on simple devices with only a single report per type (input, output, feature), the report ID is omitted. I suppose we should add a field \"id\" stating the report ID.",
      "parentUuid": "553711bf_6fd9c099",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 123,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 123,
        "endChar": 65
      },
